artifacts.enantiomorph_translation:
**9:15** And the one tongue prepared for whispering was loosened, to name the one thing that had received no name; and the number of its words was not counted, because each word came into being before its own beginning;

**9:16** I heard only the between of them, and the between was a place; and the place planted itself; and so I saw the tongue growing in the vision, and the one seated upon it,
having hands opening like petals and eyes stretched toward the ground from which he was rising;

**9:17** and his head was the head of a bud,
and from his mouth there issued one unfinished word,
and the word took root in the air, and the air put forth shoots; and the unfinished was its seed.
